{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Proposition 0.1 on RP^2 at p = 2: if a in H^n(X; Z) generates a Z summand, then abar = j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r^n and not in im d_r^(n-1), for every r >= 1\n  stable from page 2: i_2 is injective in every degree, so k_2 = 0, d_r = 0 and E_r = E_2 for every r >= 2 (E_inf = E_2)\n  n = 0: H^0 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_1^0 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_2^0 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 1: H^1 = 0 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_1^1 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_2^1 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  n = 2: H^2 = Z/2 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_1^2 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_2^2 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  why this is complete: a generates a Z summand of H iff its class in H/T(H) is primitive; psi_r(a) = [j_r(p^(r-1) a)] in E_r^n / im d_r^(n-1) vanishes iff a is in K = ker psi_r, and the image of K in the free group H/T(H) contains a primitive vector iff the gcd of its coordinates (the content) is 1\n  r > 2: page 2 is stable (i_2 injective: k = 0, and i_2 is an isomorphism of exact couples onto page 3 with j_(r+1)(p^r a) = j_r(p^(r-1) a)), so every later page and every abar is the one at r = 2\n  holds for every n and every r >= 1\n  reduced: cells 1 1 1 -> 1 1 1 (unit pivots cancelled; f g = 1, 1 - g f = dh + hd and both chain maps checked on every cell)\n  check: d o d = 0 (14), d maps relations to relations (2), chain map commutes with d (6), induced map well defined (28), exact (36), short exact (degree) (3), snake lemma lift (2), stable page: d = 0, next page equal (3), reduction: f g = 1, 1 - g f = dh + hd, chain maps (1)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "prop01", "ucas": "prop01 RP^2 mod 2 pages 3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "prop01", "space": "RP^2", "p": 2, "stable_page": 2, "degrees": [{"degree": 0, "H": "Z", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "2", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}, {"degree": 1, "H": "0", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}, {"degree": 2, "H": "Z/2", "pages": [{"page": 1, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}, {"page": 2, "in_ker": true, "content": "0", "not_in_im": true, "holds": true}]}], "holds": true, "reduced": {"cells_before": [1, 1, 1], "cells_after": [1, 1, 1]}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "d o d = 0", "points": 14, "passed": true, "text": "d o d = 0: verified 14 times"}, {"kind": "d maps relations to relations", "points": 2, "passed": true, "text": "d maps relations to relations: verified 2 times"}, {"kind": "chain map commutes with d", "points": 6, "passed": true, "text": "chain map commutes with d: verified 6 times"}, {"kind": "induced map well defined", "points": 28, "passed": true, "text": "induced map well defined: verified 28 times"}, {"kind": "exact", "points": 36, "passed": true, "text": "exact: verified 36 times"}, {"kind": "short exact (degree)", "points": 3, "passed": true, "text": "short exact (degree): verified 3 times"}, {"kind": "snake lemma lift", "points": 2, "passed": true, "text": "snake lemma lift: verified 2 times"}, {"kind": "stable page: d = 0, next page equal", "points": 3, "passed": true, "text": "stable page: d = 0, next page equal: verified 3 times"}, {"kind": "reduction: f g = 1, 1 - g f = dh + hd, chain maps", "points": 1, "passed": true, "text": "reduction: f g = 1, 1 - g f = dh + hd, chain maps: verified 1 times"}], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "checked for every degree and every page up to the stable one; later pages are isomorphic to it"}, "files": [], "text": "Proposition 0.1 on RP^2 at p = 2: if a in H^n(X; Z) generates a Z summand, then abar = j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r^n and not in im d_r^(n-1), for every r >= 1\n  stable from page 2: i_2 is injective in every degree, so k_2 = 0, d_r = 0 and E_r = E_2 for every r >= 2 (E_inf = E_2)\n  n = 0: H^0 = Z\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_1^0 / im d_1) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^0 [ok]; ker(H^0 -> E_2^0 / im d_2) has content 2 != 1 [ok]\n  n = 1: H^1 = 0 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_1^1 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^1 [ok]; ker(H^1 -> E_2^1 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  n = 2: H^2 = Z/2 (no Z summand: nothing to prove; checked anyway)\n    r = 1: d_1 j_1 2^0 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_1^2 / im d_1) has content 0 [vacuous]\n    r = 2: d_2 j_2 2^1 = 0 on H^2 [ok]; ker(H^2 -> E_2^2 / im d_2) has content 0 [vacuous]\n  why this is complete: a generates a Z summand of H iff its class in H/T(H) is primitive; psi_r(a) = [j_r(p^(r-1) a)] in E_r^n / im d_r^(n-1) vanishes iff a is in K = ker psi_r, and the image of K in the free group H/T(H) contains a primitive vector iff the gcd of its coordinates (the content) is 1\n  r > 2: page 2 is stable (i_2 injective: k = 0, and i_2 is an isomorphism of exact couples onto page 3 with j_(r+1)(p^r a) = j_r(p^(r-1) a)), so every later page and every abar is the one at r = 2\n  holds for every n and every r >= 1\n  reduced: cells 1 1 1 -> 1 1 1 (unit pivots cancelled; f g = 1, 1 - g f = dh + hd and both chain maps checked on every cell)\n  check: d o d = 0 (14), d maps relations to relations (2), chain map commutes with d (6), induced map well defined (28), exact (36), short exact (degree) (3), snake lemma lift (2), stable page: d = 0, next page equal (3), reduction: f g = 1, 1 - g f = dh + hd, chain maps (1)\n"}, "isError": false}}
